<title>RUSSIA: Russian Zaveryukha sees net harvest up to 72 mln T.</title>
<headline>Russian Zaveryukha sees net harvest up to 72 mln T.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1996-10-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deputy Prime Minister Alexander Zaveryukha, in charge of the harvest, sees Russia's 1996 net grain harvest at up to 72 million tonnes, Interfax news agency quoted him as saying on Tuesday.</p>
<p>It quoted Zaveryukha as telling grain producers in the Siberian city of Omsk that gross (bunker weight) grain output this year would be 85 million tonnes.</p>
</text>
